// Pinned Public Suffix List used by M10 identifier normalisation (TS and Python read this
// same file; see LLD M10 "Normalisation spec").
//
// Format: https://publicsuffix.org/list/ — one rule per line, "//" comments, "*." wildcard
// rules, "!" exception rules. Rules are matched label by label, right to left. When no rule
// matches, the implicit rule "*" applies (the TLD is the public suffix), so every plain TLD
// (.com, .de, .io, ...) works without being listed; only multi-label suffixes must appear.
//
// PIN: m10-psl-2026-09-25. This snapshot carries the multi-label ICANN suffixes of the
// markets the product covers plus common private hosting suffixes. Replacing it with a newer
// upstream snapshot is a data change that re-keys some hashes: bump the pin, re-run the shared
// vectors in both languages, and re-project (m09.project) before deploying.

